  <v1.6>
    <li>/</li>
    <li>1.6</li>
    <!-- Facial Animation heads: NL-style painted head, or the vanilla-style baked heads when VTE supplies vanilla-styled faces. -->
    <li IfModNotActive="VanillaExpanded.VTEXE.FacialAnims">1.6/Mods/NoVTEFacialAnimation</li>
    <li IfModActive="VanillaExpanded.VTEXE.FacialAnims">1.6/Mods/VTEFacialAnimation</li>
    <!--
      Body mod folders. Exactly ONE loads: each folder is disallowed whenever a higher-priority
      body mod is active, so precedence is explicit and does not depend on patch order.

      Patch order within this mod: RimWorld walks this list BACKWARDS, so patch files in the
      LAST entry are applied FIRST and the root 1.6/Patches run after every Mods/ folder. Patch
      files are also keyed by their path relative to each folder, so two folders must not both
      contain e.g. Patches/Foo.xml - only one of them would load.

      Priority, highest first:
        1. Sized Apparel        - swaps the base body to its own shape; its fur art is what fits
        2. Yttakin retexture    - a deliberate, specific furskin replacement
        3. VRE NL Compatible Body 2 - generic NL body set, overrides vanilla FurCovered paths
        4. Scrubdaddy's Bodies  - generic body set, overrides vanilla FurCovered paths
    -->
    <li IfModActive="OTYOTY.SizedApparel">1.6/Mods/SizedApparel</li>
    <li IfModActive="ChenDuXiu.Gene.MoreCuteYttakin"
        IfModNotActive="OTYOTY.SizedApparel">1.6/Mods/Yttakin</li>
    <li IfModActive="Mainrrow.VRECompatibleBody2"
        IfModNotActive="OTYOTY.SizedApparel,ChenDuXiu.Gene.MoreCuteYttakin">1.6/Mods/VRECompatibleBody2</li>
    <li IfModActive="ScrubDaddy.Bodies"
        IfModNotActive="OTYOTY.SizedApparel,ChenDuXiu.Gene.MoreCuteYttakin,Mainrrow.VRECompatibleBody2">1.6/Mods/ScrubDaddy</li>
  </v1.6>
</loadFolders>
